{
  "kanji": "両",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 両\ntitle: both\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 6\nradical: 一\nradicalNumber: 1\nonyomi: [リョウ]\nkunyomi: [てる, ふたつ]\ndistractors: [雨, 内, 西]\n---\n\n# 両 — both\n\n**Strokes:** 6 · **Key (radical):** 一 (no. 1) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n両 brings two sides or members of a pair into view together. In [両方](../words/両方.md) りょうほう, neither side is excluded;\n両手 りょうて means both hands.\nDo not use \"both\" as a general replacement for \"all\" when more than two independent items are meant.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** see two inner uprights sheltered by one broad top line: both belong under the same cover.\nThis describes the modern shape, not its origin.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| リョウ | on | [両方](../words/両方.md) りょうほう — both; 両手 りょうて — both hands |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [両方](../words/両方.md) りょうほう — both; both sides\n- 両手 りょうて — both hands\n\n## Notes\n\nThe boxed silhouettes of [雨](雨.md), [内](内.md), and [西](西.md) can distract the eye.\nCheck the interior rather than treating every broad frame as the same character.\n両 also occurs in historical currency and vehicle-counting uses; the pair meaning is the focus here.\nThe source's kun readings are preserved in metadata, not recommended as substitutes for リョウ in these words.\n",
